; claude: the terminal, from scratch: Vt (the VT100's screen, the
; bytes a program writes turned into a grid of cells) and
; Line_discipline (the tty between the keyboard and the program:
; echo, Backspace, a line on Enter). Pure OCaml, bytes in and bytes
; out, no Playground: the Teletype way and TinyTerminal are built on
; it. Talk: the programs that ask and wait, as values, and the machine
; playing one on a Vt (BASIC's, the teletype games', TinyTerminal's). And Curses (a screen drawn whole, sent as what changed) and Tui (a
; full-screen program, Model-View-Update), which the Textmode way runs
; on the playground and unix/'s Tty_unix in a real terminal. See
; docs/claude_notes/plans/plan_terminal.md.
(library
 (name terminal)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries random) ; Lehmer, Talk's seeded numbers
)
